<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Computing - Spreadsheet Applications Quiz</title>
<style>
body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background:#f2f5f8;margin:0;padding:20px}
.container{max-width:800px;margin:auto;background:white;padding:25px;border-radius:15px;box-shadow:0 3px 15px #bbb}
h1{text-align:center;color:#1f4e79}
.question{margin:22px 0;padding:18px;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:10px}
.option{display:block;margin:9px 0;padding:12px;background:#f7f7f7;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer}
button{width:100%;padding:15px;background:#1f4e79;color:white;border:0;border-radius:10px;font-size:17px}
#result{text-align:center;font-size:22px;font-weight:bold;margin-top:20px}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
<h1>Computing: Spreadsheet Applications</h1>
<p><b>30 Objective Questions</b> — Choose A, B, C or D.</p>
<form id="quiz">
<div class="question"><b>1. Which is the main working area in a spreadsheet where data is entered?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="A"> A. Worksheet</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="B"> B. Slide</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="C"> C. Database</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="D"> D. Document</label></div><div class="question"><b>2. The intersection of a row and a column is called a:</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="A"> A. Cell</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="B"> B. Range</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="C"> C. Workbook</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="D"> D. Record</label></div><div class="question"><b>3. Which formula adds values from A1 to A5?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="A"> A. =SUM(A1:A5)</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="B"> B. =ADD(A1:A5)</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="C"> C. =TOTAL(A1:A5)</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="D"> D. =PLUS(A1:A5)</label></div><div class="question"><b>4. Which feature arranges data alphabetically or numerically?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="A"> A. Sorting</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="B"> B. Filtering</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="C"> C. Formatting</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="D"> D. Merging</label></div><div class="question"><b>5. Which function calculates the arithmetic mean?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q5" value="A"> A. COUNT</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q5" value="B"> B. AVERAGE</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q5" value="C"> C. MAX</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q5" value="D"> D. MIN</label></div><div class="question"><b>6. What does the cell reference B7 identify?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q6" value="A"> A. Column B, row 7</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q6" value="B"> B. Row B, column 7</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q6" value="C"> C. Column 7, row B</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q6" value="D"> D. Worksheet B, cell 7</label></div><div class="question"><b>7. Which symbol normally begins a spreadsheet formula?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q7" value="A"> A. =</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q7" value="B"> B. #</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q7" value="C"> C. @</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q7" value="D"> D. &</label></div><div class="question"><b>8. Which function returns the largest value in a range?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q8" value="A"> A. MIN</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q8" value="B"> B. MAX</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q8" value="C"> C. AVERAGE</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q8" value="D"> D. COUNT</label></div><div class="question"><b>9. A group of selected cells is called a:</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q9" value="A"> A. Range</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q9" value="B"> B. Record</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q9" value="C"> C. Chart</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q9" value="D"> D. Slide</label></div><div class="question"><b>10. Which chart is commonly used to show changes over time?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q10" value="A"> A. Line chart</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q10" value="B"> B. Pie chart</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q10" value="C"> C. Radar chart</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q10" value="D"> D. Picture chart</label></div><div class="question"><b>11. Which feature displays only rows that meet specified conditions?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q11" value="A"> A. Filtering</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q11" value="B"> B. Sorting</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q11" value="C"> C. Merging</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q11" value="D"> D. Wrapping</label></div><div class="question"><b>12. What does =A1+B1 do?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q12" value="A"> A. Adds A1 and B1</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q12" value="B"> B. Multiplies A1 and B1</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q12" value="C"> C. Divides A1 by B1</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q12" value="D"> D. Subtracts B1 from A1</label></div><div class="question"><b>13. Which feature can extend a series such as 1, 2, 3, 4?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q13" value="A"> A. AutoFill</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q13" value="B"> B. Spell Check</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q13" value="C"> C. Page Break</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q13" value="D"> D. Freeze Panes</label></div><div class="question"><b>14. Which function counts cells containing numbers?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q14" value="A"> A. COUNT</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q14" value="B"> B. SUM</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q14" value="C"> C. MAX</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q14" value="D"> D. AVERAGE</label></div><div class="question"><b>15. What is the main purpose of a spreadsheet formula?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q15" value="A"> A. To perform calculations using data</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q15" value="B"> B. To create computer hardware</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q15" value="C"> C. To connect a printer</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q15" value="D"> D. To replace the operating system</label></div><div class="question"><b>16. Which is an absolute cell reference?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q16" value="A"> A. $A$1</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q16" value="B"> B. A1</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q16" value="C"> C. A$1</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q16" value="D"> D. $A1</label></div><div class="question"><b>17. What does the asterisk (*) represent in a spreadsheet formula?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q17" value="A"> A. Multiplication</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q17" value="B"> B. Addition</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q17" value="C"> C. Subtraction</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q17" value="D"> D. Division</label></div><div class="question"><b>18. Which feature keeps selected rows or columns visible while scrolling?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q18" value="A"> A. Freeze Panes</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q18" value="B"> B. AutoSum</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q18" value="C"> C. Data Validation</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q18" value="D"> D. Page Setup</label></div><div class="question"><b>19. Which feature changes cell appearance when a condition is met?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q19" value="A"> A. Conditional Formatting</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q19" value="B"> B. AutoFill</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q19" value="C"> C. Sorting</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q19" value="D"> D. Page Setup</label></div><div class="question"><b>20. A1 contains 20, A2 contains 30, A3 contains 40 and A4 contains 50. What is =SUM(A1:A4)?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q20" value="A"> A. 120</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q20" value="B"> B. 130</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q20" value="C"> C. 140</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q20" value="D"> D. 150</label></div><div class="question"><b>21. Which function returns the smallest value in a range?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q21" value="A"> A. MIN</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q21" value="B"> B. MAX</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q21" value="C"> C. COUNT</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q21" value="D"> D. SUM</label></div><div class="question"><b>22. Which operator is used for division in most spreadsheets?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q22" value="A"> A. +</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q22" value="B"> B. -</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q22" value="C"> C. *</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q22" value="D"> D. /</label></div><div class="question"><b>23. What does a workbook normally contain?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q23" value="A"> A. One or more worksheets</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q23" value="B"> B. Only charts</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q23" value="C"> C. Only formulas</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q23" value="D"> D. Only text documents</label></div><div class="question"><b>24. Which command combines two or more cells into one larger cell?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q24" value="A"> A. Merge Cells</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q24" value="B"> B. Freeze Panes</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q24" value="C"> C. Sort</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q24" value="D"> D. Filter</label></div><div class="question"><b>25. Which feature restricts the type of data that can be entered into a cell?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q25" value="A"> A. Data Validation</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q25" value="B"> B. Conditional Formatting</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q25" value="C"> C. AutoFill</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q25" value="D"> D. Sorting</label></div><div class="question"><b>26. What is the result of =10*5?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q26" value="A"> A. 15</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q26" value="B"> B. 50</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q26" value="C"> C. 100</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q26" value="D"> D. 500</label></div><div class="question"><b>27. Which function adds a selected range of numerical values?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q27" value="A"> A. SUM</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q27" value="B"> B. COUNT</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q27" value="C"> C. MIN</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q27" value="D"> D. AVERAGE</label></div><div class="question"><b>28. What does a relative cell reference do when a formula is copied?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q28" value="A"> A. It can change according to its new position</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q28" value="B"> B. It always remains fixed</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q28" value="C"> C. It deletes the formula</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q28" value="D"> D. It changes into a chart</label></div><div class="question"><b>29. Which chart is commonly used to show parts of a whole?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q29" value="A"> A. Pie chart</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q29" value="B"> B. Line chart</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q29" value="C"> C. Scatter chart</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q29" value="D"> D. Area chart</label></div><div class="question"><b>30. What is the purpose of a spreadsheet chart?</b><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q30" value="A"> A. To represent data graphically</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q30" value="B"> B. To delete worksheet data</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q30" value="C"> C. To protect a computer from viruses</label><label class="option"><input type="radio" name="q30" value="D"> D. To replace formulas</label></div>
<button type="button" onclick="markQuiz()">Submit Quiz</button>
</form>
<div id="result"></div>
</div>
<script>
const answers = ['A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'B', 'A', 'A', 'B', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'C', 'A', 'D', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'B', 'A', 'A', 'A', 'A'];
function markQuiz(){
 let score=0;
 answers.forEach((ans,i)=>{
   const chosen=document.querySelector('input[name="q'+(i+1)+'"]:checked');
   if(chosen && chosen.value===ans) score++;
 });
 document.getElementById('result').innerHTML =
   "Your Score: "+score+" / "+answers.length+
   "<br><small>"+Math.round(score/answers.length*100)+"%</small>";
 window.scrollTo(0,document.body.scrollHeight);
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
